    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0348" n="1182" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/484½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the War Trade Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >McCormick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Norwegian
                        Minister on Special Mission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Nansen</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 30, 1918</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Referring to an agreement between the
                    War Trade Board and the Norwegian Government by you as its special
                    representative, we beg to assure you that notwithstanding the limitation “at
                    ports of origin” contained in section 2 of article 1 of said agreement, Norway
                    shall be entitled to receive her estimated needs <pb facs="0349" n="1183"
                        xml:id="pg1183"/> at her own ports in accordance with the other terms of
                    said contract. Nothing herein or in said contract however to be construed as an
                    obligation on the part of the United States or her associates in the war to
                    furnish Norway the tonnage to lift the commodities included as her needs.</p>
                <p>Yours very truly,</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vance C. McCormick</hi>
                        </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
